& [AlienHandIRCChatPlatform] is the bounded chat substrate for AI-user conversation inside AlienHand apps
  + [purpose] is to host persistent channel conversation between users and AI agents while preserving full replayable context
  + [app_instance] is one running AlienHand app using chat
  + [app_id] is a compact app-scoped identifier, expected to fit in 64 bits
  + [irc_server] is Ergo running inside the lifecycle of [app_instance]
  + [human_client] is thelounge adapted as the human-facing chat surface
  + [ai_client] is one independent IRC client connection for one AI agent identity
  + [channel] is a 32-character UUID-hex-named IRC channel whose topic stores the human-readable conversation description
  + [message_envelope] is the compact IRC-delivered reference to a message payload
  + [message_payload] is the rich message object fetched by UUID from the payload resolver or read from the payload store
  + [channel_history] is append-only JSONL scoped to one channel UUID
  + [payload_store] is durable immutable storage for payload objects
  + [payload_resolver] is the service API that resolves message UUIDs into rich renderable payloads
  + [context_replay] is chunked back-fill of channel history for AI context reconstruction or user history commands
  + [ephemeral_pm_context] is private-message context retained only for a live user session when needed by AI
  + [resolution] is proceed_to_design_after_protocol_review

  = must: start [irc_server] whenever [app_instance] starts and chat is enabled
  = must: connect each AI agent through its own [ai_client]
  = must: use [channel] UUID as stable identity and topic text as mutable description
  = must: keep IRC delivery compact and delegate rich content to [payload_store] and [payload_resolver]
  = must: store durable channel events as JSONL
  = must: replay channel history from JSONL and payload files, not from live IRC memory alone
  = must: preserve uncertainty where command syntax, chunk sizing, and retention policy remain open
  - never: treat the IRC line as the rich content payload
  - never: treat channel topic as channel identity
  - never: persist private messages by default

## Boundary

/ [AlienHandIRCChatPlatform] -(Delineation)> [inside], [outside], [references], [uncertainty]

& [ChatPlatformBoundary] is the subject boundary for the current planning stage
  + [inside] is app-owned IRC lifecycle, AI IRC identities, channel UUIDs, envelope format, payload storage, payload resolution, commit order, JSONL channel logs, replay, and rich client rendering contracts
  + [outside] is emulator control, game automation policy, model prompting policy, account federation, public IRC network operation, and production deployment hardening
  + [references] are Ergo, thelounge, BizHawk, SOP platform docs, and existing AlienHand AI telemetry/context systems
  + [uncertainty] is history command syntax, payload directory layout, access control, PM retention timeout, message chunk size, and exact thelounge extension strategy

  = must: keep implementation work blocked until the subject contract is reviewed
  = must: preserve [outside] as adjacent but not fused into the chat substrate
  = must: move [uncertainty] into progress nodes rather than hiding it in prose

## Identity Vocabulary

| [ChatActorType] is (user | ai_agent | system | service)
| [MessageEventType] is (message | action | join | part | nick_change | topic_change | history_request | system_note | ai_observation | ai_response | payload_error)
| [PayloadKind] is (text | rich_text | code | image | file | link | mixed | system)
| [PersistenceScope] is (durable_channel | ephemeral_session | service_cache)
| [ProgressState] is (not_started | specified | prototype_ready | in_progress | blocked | verified | deferred)
| [ReplayDirection] is (recent_first_backfill | oldest_first_reconstruct)

& [ChannelIdentity] is the stable conversation identity
  + [channel_uuid] is the 32-character lowercase hexadecimal UUID value
  + [irc_channel_name] is "#" plus [channel_uuid], with expected length 33
  + [topic] is the human-readable conversation description
  + [history_path] is the durable JSONL stream for [channel_uuid]
  + [payload_index] is the set of message UUIDs referenced by [history_path]

  = must: use [channel_uuid] for routing, storage, replay, and identity
  = must: normalize hyphenated UUID text into 32-character lowercase hex before persistence or IRC publication
  = must: publish IRC channel targets as [irc_channel_name]
  = must: allow [topic] to change without changing identity
  - never: infer identity from topic text

& [AIClientIdentity] is the network-visible identity of one AI agent
  + [agent_id] is the stable AlienHand AI identity
  + [nick] is the IRC-visible nickname
  + [connection] is the agent's dedicated IRC client session
  + [actor_type] is ai_agent

  = must: allocate one [connection] per active AI agent
  = must: preserve attribution per [agent_id]
  = must: avoid shared bot identity for multiple agents

## IRC Envelope

& [IRCMessageEnvelope] is the compact line payload sent through IRC for one rich message
  + [protocol] is AHIRC/1
  + [app_id] is compact 64-bit app identifier
  + [channel_uuid] is the 32-character channel identity
  + [message_uuid] is the payload and history event identity
  + [nick] is the sender nick at send time
  + [timestamp] is UTC date-time with milliseconds
  + [wire_form] is a compact token sequence carried in the IRC message body

  = must: include [app_id], [channel_uuid], [message_uuid], [nick], and [timestamp]
  = must: stay boring and parseable
  = must: keep [wire_form] below a conservative IRC body budget before server framing
  = must: allow the client to render a placeholder while resolving [message_uuid]
  = must: use 32-character lowercase UUID hex for [channel_uuid]
  = should: use a fixed timestamp form such as YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS.mmmZ
  = should: keep field labels short if labels are used
  - never: include rich message content in [wire_form]
  - never: embed JSON in [wire_form]
  - never: use [wire_form] to hide command payloads

! [EnvelopeBudget] is acceptable for the current metadata set
  @ [support] one 32-character channel UUID hex value, one message UUID, one 64-bit app id, nick, and millisecond timestamp fit comfortably under the common IRC 512-byte line budget when the message body remains compact

~ [EnvelopeWireForm] is provisional
  + [candidate] is "AH1 a=<app_id> c=<32_char_channel_uuid_hex> m=<message_uuid> n=<nick> t=<YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS.mmmZ>"
  + [reason] is readable compactness while preserving direct debugging value

## Payload Store And Resolver

& [PayloadStore] is durable immutable storage for payload objects
  + [message_uuid] is the lookup key and payload identity
  + [payload_file] is the stored rich message object
  + [durability] is confirmed enough for prototype replay before IRC publication
  + [immutability] is the rule that payload files are not rewritten once referenced

  = must: write [PayloadObject] before [IRCMessageEnvelope] publication
  = must: preserve payloads independently of resolver process availability
  = must: allow cold replay to read stored payloads directly
  = must: make missing payloads observable as payload_error rather than silent loss
  = should: keep payload files immutable once referenced by durable history

& [PayloadResolver] is the service API that resolves message UUIDs into renderable payloads
  + [message_uuid] is the lookup key
  + [payload_store] is [PayloadStore]
  + [payload_kind] is one [PayloadKind]
  + [attachments] are linked media or files referenced by the payload
  + [render_model] is the normalized structure consumed by the chat client
  + [cache_policy] is the local client and service caching rule

  = must: return payload data by [message_uuid]
  = must: read from [PayloadStore]
  = must: support text, rich text, code frames, image frames, links, files, and mixed payloads
  = must: return a structured error payload when [message_uuid] cannot be resolved
  = should: normalize payloads into a render model without becoming the durability owner

& [PayloadObject] is the canonical rich message data resolved by [PayloadResolver] or read directly from [PayloadStore]
  + [message_uuid] is stable identity
  + [app_id] is source app identity
  + [channel_uuid] is source channel identity
  + [sender] is sender nick or stable actor id
  + [sender_type] is one [ChatActorType]
  + [event_type] is one [MessageEventType]
  + [payload_kind] is one [PayloadKind]
  + [created_at] is UTC timestamp with milliseconds
  + [content] is the rich content body
  + [frames] are code, image, file, link, or mixed media render units
  + [metadata] is optional structured support data

  = must: be sufficient for client rendering without depending on the IRC line after lookup
  = must: be sufficient for AI replay after lookup
  = must: preserve sender, channel, timestamp, event type, payload kind, and content metadata

## Commit Order

& [MessageCommitOrder] is the durability ordering for one message
  + [message_uuid] is allocated before durable writes
  + [payload_write] is writing [PayloadObject] into [PayloadStore]
  + [payload_durability] is confirmation that [payload_write] is durable enough for prototype replay
  + [history_append] is appending the channel JSONL event
  + [irc_publish] is publishing [IRCMessageEnvelope] after durable state exists

  = must: allocate [message_uuid]
  = must: write [PayloadObject]
  = must: confirm [payload_durability] within prototype scope
  = must: append [ChannelJSONLHistory] event
  = must: publish [IRCMessageEnvelope] only after payload and history writes succeed
  ? [IRC publish succeeds but client payload lookup fails]
    = must: render placeholder or payload_error
  ? [payload write fails]
    = must: block [irc_publish]
  ? [history_append fails]
    = must: block [irc_publish]
    = must: preserve failed write state for inspection if payload already exists

  - never: depend on live IRC memory for replay success

## Durable History

& [ChannelJSONLHistory] is the durable append-only event stream for one channel
  + [scope] is durable_channel
  + [channel_uuid] is the owning channel
  + [event] is one JSON object per line
  + [message_uuid] links to [PayloadObject] when the event has payload content
  + [ordering] is timestamp plus append order

  = must: append channel events without rewriting history
  = must: record history requests as structured events
  = must: preserve enough metadata to rebuild channel context from cold start
  = should: include both [message_uuid] and [timestamp] for replay ordering

## Replay And Context

& [ChannelContextReplay] is the chunked recovery of prior channel messages
  + [source] is [ChannelJSONLHistory]
  + [payload_resolver] is [PayloadResolver]
  + [payload_store] is [PayloadStore]
  + [direction] is recent_first_backfill by default
  + [chunk] is a bounded set of history events and payloads
  + [consumer] is AI context loader or user history command handler
  + [stop_condition] is request fulfilled, context budget reached, or source exhausted

  = must: back-fill full previous messages in chunks
  = must: resolve message payloads by UUID during replay
  = must: read [PayloadStore] directly when [PayloadResolver] is unavailable
  = must: preserve chronological reconstruction when presenting history
  = must: expose missing payloads as payload_error events
  = should: load recent chunks first for AI usefulness, then expand backward as needed

& [HistoryCommand] is the user-triggered request for channel history
  + [syntax] is unresolved
  + [channel_uuid] is the current channel identity
  + [requester] is the user nick or actor id
  + [range] is requested chunk count, message count, time span, or all
  + [response_mode] is unresolved

  ? [syntax is selected]
    = must: parse before normal AI response generation
    = must: record [history_request] as a payload-backed structured event
    = must: call [ChannelContextReplay]

  ~ [syntax] is provisional until the client command model is chosen

## Ephemeral Private Messages

& [EphemeralPMContext] is the live private-message context available to AI during a user session
  + [scope] is ephemeral_session
  + [user_session] is the active private-message relation
  + [consumer] is an AI agent context window
  + [retention] is until disconnect or session expiry

  = may: feed live AI context while the user remains connected
  = must: dispose when [user_session] ends or expires
  = must: stay outside durable per-channel JSONL history
  - never: persist PMs by default

## Client Rendering

& [RichChatClientSurface] is the adapted thelounge channel perspective for AlienHand chat
  + [left_bubble] is user-originated message rendering
  + [right_bubble] is AI-agent-originated message rendering
  + [system_row] is system or service event rendering
  + [code_frame] is framed code rendering with language metadata when available
  + [image_frame] is framed image rendering from linked media
  + [media_frame] is linked file, link, or mixed payload rendering
  + [placeholder] is the temporary UI for unresolved payload UUIDs

  = must: render users left-oriented and AI agents right-oriented
  = must: render rich payloads from [PayloadObject], not from IRC text content
  = must: support code frames, image frames, linked media, and rich text or equivalent structured formatting
  = must: show graceful unresolved-payload state
  = should: remain deferred until envelope delivery, payload lookup, and cold replay are verified

## Protocol Review

& [ChatPlatformProtocolReview] is the blocking review before implementation
  + [review_targets] are envelope, commit order, replay semantics, payload errors, identity, and PM retention
  + [acceptance] is smallest prototype contract approved
  + [minimum_payload_schema] is the smallest [PayloadObject] that can render and replay one message
  + [minimum_history_schema] is the smallest [ChannelJSONLHistory] event that can cold-replay one channel
  + [cold_replay_acceptance_test] is restarting with no live IRC memory and reconstructing the channel from JSONL plus payload files

  = must: resolve write ordering
  = must: choose [minimum_payload_schema]
  = must: choose [minimum_history_schema]
  = must: choose [cold_replay_acceptance_test]
  = must: leave thelounge rich rendering deferred

& [AlienHandIRCTruthTest] is the smallest end-to-end proof of the chat substrate
  + [one_app] is one AlienHand app instance
  + [one_ergo] is one local Ergo server
  + [one_channel] is one 32-character UUID-hex-named channel
  + [one_user_client] is thelounge or a minimal IRC client
  + [one_ai_client] is one independent AI IRC connection
  + [one_payload_store] is durable payload object storage
  + [one_payload_resolver] resolves message UUID to payload JSON
  + [one_history_file] is append-only JSONL for the channel

  = must: start Ergo with app lifecycle
  = must: send AHIRC/1 envelope through IRC
  = must: write payload object before or atomically with envelope publication
  = must: append JSONL event for the channel
  = must: resolve payload by message UUID
  = must: cold-replay channel context after restart
  = must: show unresolved payload as explicit payload_error
  - never: depend on live IRC memory for replay success

## Integration Assessment

& [ChatPlatformIntegration] is the current feasibility and path assessment
  + [concept] is [AlienHandIRCChatPlatform]
  + [available_support] is Ergo submodule, thelounge submodule, AlienHand Python AI layer, existing JSONL run artifacts, and current docs
  + [missing_support] is user IRC client proof, thelounge render adaptation, access control, and production lifecycle hardening
  + [hidden_constraints] are IRC framing limits, authentication, service discovery, client extension strategy, concurrent writes, payload immutability, and cross-app isolation
  + [feasibility_gradient] is prototypeable
  + [next_step] is [ChatPlatformProtocolReview] followed by [AlienHandIRCTruthTest]

  = must: prototype before broad UI customization
  = must: validate envelope delivery and payload lookup before rich rendering
  = must: validate replay from cold JSONL before AI context claims are made

## Sierpinski Work Graph

& [ChatPlatformProgressGraph] is the staged convergence graph for tracking heavy work
  + [root_goal] is stable AI-user chat with IRC delivery, rich payload rendering, and replayable context
  + [identity_node] is channel/app/actor/message identity
  + [transport_node] is IRC envelope delivery
  + [irc_publisher_node] is socket-level IRC registration, join, and envelope PRIVMSG publication
  + [payload_store_node] is file-backed rich message durability
  + [payload_resolver_node] is message UUID lookup and render normalization
  + [commit_order_node] is message write ordering before IRC publication
  + [history_node] is per-channel JSONL append and replay
  + [protocol_review_node] is the blocking review before implementation
  + [truth_test_core_node] is the executable substrate proof before real Ergo transport
  + [truth_test_node] is the smallest end-to-end proof
  + [lifecycle_node] is local Ergo startup and shutdown
  + [app_lifecycle_node] is AlienHand app-owned Ergo startup and shutdown
  + [client_node] is thelounge bubble and frame rendering
  + [ai_node] is one AI connection per agent plus context replay
  + [pm_node] is ephemeral private-message context
  + [security_node] is auth, isolation, access control, and data exposure policy
  + [resolution] is rerun_required until prototype tests verify child nodes

  = must: resolve child nodes before claiming parent convergence
  = must: backpropagate failures to the earliest unstable node
  = must: update boundary, priority, or decomposition before rerunning a failed pass

& [ProgressStatus] is the current tracked state of each work node
  + [identity_node] is specified
  + [transport_node] is in_progress
  + [irc_publisher_node] is verified_against_fake_server
  + [payload_store_node] is verified
  + [payload_resolver_node] is verified
  + [commit_order_node] is verified
  + [history_node] is verified
  + [protocol_review_node] is specified
  + [truth_test_core_node] is verified
  + [truth_test_node] is in_progress
  + [lifecycle_node] is verified_local_ergo
  + [app_lifecycle_node] is verified_app_service_proof
  + [client_node] is deferred
  + [ai_node] is not_started
  + [pm_node] is specified
  + [security_node] is deferred

  ? [prototype begins]
    = must: move only the active node to in_progress
    = must: leave unimplemented nodes visible

& [RuntimePrototypeSlice] is the implemented first slice of [AlienHandIRCTruthTest]
  + [implemented_artifact] is AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/chat_platform.py
  + [test_artifact] is AlienHand/python/tests/test_chat_platform.py
  + [cli_entry] is "python -m alienhand_ai.cli chat-truth-test --output runs --name chat-truth-test"
  + [cli_entry] is "python -m alienhand_ai.cli chat-irc-publish --host 127.0.0.1 --port 6667 --nick alienhand-agent"
  + [cli_entry] is "python -m alienhand_ai.cli chat-ergo-proof --output runs --name chat-ergo-proof"
  + [cli_entry] is "python -m alienhand_ai.cli chat-app-lifecycle-proof --output runs --name chat-app-lifecycle-proof"
  + [verified_behavior] is AH1 envelope round-trip, 32-character channel UUID hex normalization, payload durability, JSONL append, blocked publication on history failure, cold replay, payload_error on missing payload, socket-level IRC JOIN/PRIVMSG publication against a fake server, real local Ergo startup/publication/shutdown, and AlienHand-owned service lifecycle startup/publication/shutdown
  + [remaining_truth_test] is one real user client and thelounge payload rendering

  = must: treat this as verified local proof, not as complete user-facing chat integration
  = must: use this slice as the base for the next user-client and rich-rendering steps

## Dual-Hemisphere Settlement

& [DualHemisphereSettlement] is the current balanced interpretation of the design
  + [master_pattern] is IRC as narrow live coordination while the real chat substrate is the subject graph of channel UUIDs, JSONL history, immutable payload files, and replay
  + [emissary_structure] is envelope, commit order, payload store, payload resolver, history, replay, rendering, and lifecycle contracts
  + [friction] is the risk that this becomes over-complex before the smallest truth test
  + [convergence_notice] is that the architecture is coherent if the first prototype proves durability and replay before UI richness
  + [uncertainty] is command syntax, access control, file layout, and thelounge adaptation path

  = must: keep the living chat experience as the final purpose
  = must: let the compact protocol serve that purpose without becoming the whole system
  = must: run the smallest truth test before expanding rich UI work
